# Redoubt extension-update-controls.patch  (Android, LW-M7-35)
#
# 157 rebase (Firefox 157.0, was 153.4.0esr). What moved upstream:
#   - modules/libpref/Preferences.cpp: instance state now lives in the
#     file-private PreferencesImpl (sPImpl); SavePrefFileBlocking,
#     SavePrefFileAsync and the profile-before-change-telemetry observer use
#     sPImpl->..., WritePrefFile is PreferencesImpl::WritePrefFile, and PWRunnable
#     takes PreferencesImpl::WritePrefFilePromise. 157 already gives writes to a
#     file other than prefs.js their own snapshot; this patch still removes the
#     sPendingWriteData coalescing for prefs.js, so every write (current file,
#     explicit file, backup) owns its snapshot and its completion, as on 153.
#   - GeckoEngine.kt, AddonUpdater.kt, AddonUpdaterWorkerTest.kt: same change,
#     re-applied in upstream's reformatted (ktfmt) layout.
#   - GeckoViewStartup.sys.mjs: the WebExtension listener list is re-indented.
#   - SettingsFragment.kt: 157 no longer imports SwitchPreferenceCompat; the
#     switch lookup names it fully qualified so no import line is contested
#     with other patches.
#
# 158 rebase (2026-10-04, pre-rebase against Firefox 158.0b3): unchanged
# lines, new hunk positions only. It applied on 158 with offsets
# (geckoview/api.txt and others); the receipt replay for this hash-pinned
# patch refuses an offset, so its hunk headers now carry the in-order 158 line
# numbers.
